{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793204733,"nonce":"nZbc0PBgd80xek39m4SUhD7Rhh4=","message":"Follow-up requested by the user after cache completion: research faster LLVM WASM compilation and expose optimization choices in the CLI.\n\nCommitted ff20945c: -O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os/-Oz (--opt-level), independent --air-opt-level and --codegen-opt-level. AIR keeps its current default/environment unless explicitly overridden. CLI choices override corresponding environment settings; settings are scoped to the build and inherited by workers. Existing AotRequest/emit_aot calls remain compatible; emit_aot_with_options supplies overrides. Size attributes respect exception shields. Stripping a body now clears its personality, fixing invalid LLVM declarations found by standalone verification.\n\nLLVM 21.1.2 sources confirm that codegen 0 selects a simpler WASM register-stackification path; 1/2/3 all enable the optimizing path. Added ASH_AOT_CODEGEN_LEVEL for scripts/library use; default remains 3. Keeping AIR/LLVM IR at O3 and choosing codegen 0 is available as: ash -O3 --codegen-opt-level 0 --build app.wasm --target wasm32-wasip1-threads app.hl.\n\nValidation passed: all six -O modes plus two independent override combinations compile and run a catching program (23 expected), worker logs confirm the resolved levels, the WASM object boundary test passes, and verifier regressions cover stripped personalities and size attributes versus optnone. LLVM/no-LLVM CLI checks and cargo clippy -p ash --all-targets -- -D warnings passed.\n\nCommit recording the research: docs/wasm/llvm-build-times.md and docs/wasm/llvm-build-time-results.json. Untimed standalone LLVM replay of identical optimized IR: median codegen CPU 2.635 s at level 3 versus 0.997 s at level 0; object size 2,211,275 versus 2,427,185 bytes. Whole WindowPage paired samples: medians 34.918 s versus 23.776 s; final module 16,202,426 versus 19,742,401 bytes (+21.8%). Unrelated machine activity was observed, so whole-build samples are explicitly indicative rather than a stable CI claim. Both final modules passed headless Chrome (232/228 frames, exit 0). Runtime CPU throughput has not been established as equal, and the default stays at level 3.","files":null}]}